# What the import boundary gate installs into its own image. Two lines, and
# everything else in requirements.txt is something one of these two brought.
#
#   import-linter   the gate itself, named by rule 5 of CLAUDE.md and chosen in
#                   docs/decisions/0006-import-boundaries.md
#   grimp           the engine that builds the import graph. import-linter
#                   depends on it anyway, and it is pinned here by name because
#                   it is the compiled part and the one that decides whether an
#                   install is two seconds or forty
#
# requirements.txt beside this file is the lock, and its first two lines are the
# command that regenerates it. docs/decisions/0011-import-linter-arrives.md says
# why this gate builds an image rather than pulling one.
import-linter==2.14
grimp==3.16
